A||||14||Dave85||Recall
Z||000000||Dave85||08-18-99||07:27 PM||||Have any of you had problems getting recall work done? I bought my car from an older lady who had receipts for everything she had done. One would assume that the recall was done too. As near as I can tell it hasn't. I called the dealer and gave them the VIN and they said they had no open recalls on it.<br>  What's my next move?
Z||000001||Bruce||08-19-99||01:58 PM||||You might want to check 800 information and contact Pontiac directly. Also, they may be on the web somewhere. A dealer can't refuse to do the recall if it hasn't been completed. If they do, you can raise all sorts of hell with Pontiac
Z||000002||Dave85||08-19-99||09:14 PM||||I called the 1-800-gmcares number and they said that their computer didn't go back that far and my local dealer would be able to give me that info.  Do I really need the recall work done?
Z||000003||Bruce||08-19-99||10:23 PM||||Try 1-800-PMCARES. Someone's giving you the runaround; I bought my 86GT in May of '98 and had the work done shortly afterwards. Call another dealer, but don't give up.<br>You really should get the recall work done. It includes the new manifolds, heat shields, and emergency break retrofit. The reason for the first two was potential engine fires.<br>Look up "Pontiac Fiero" on the web and you'll find an article about the recalls. Or look under: www.alldata (or something like that).
Z||000004||theogre||08-20-99||12:02 AM|||| <A HREF="http://www.autosite.com/" TARGET=_blank>http://www.autosite.com/</A>  also has a list of NTSB/NHTSA ordered recalls back thru 1983, but they can't tell you if they were done or not.<p>Recalls DO NOT expire. if they have not been done then the dealer MUST do them. Dealers who refuse are in violation of various laws/rules, and likely their dealership agreement with GM. Any dealer who refuses to perform recall work should be reported to both GM/Pontiac and the a appropriate federal agencies.
Z||000005||Dave85||08-20-99||09:34 PM||||Thanks, I'm going to the dealer on my next day off and find out what  the problem is.<br> Dave 
Z||000006||biggdaddy||08-20-99||09:38 PM||||I`m not too familiar with the recall as I have only owned a fiero since 97. (My father owned it before since 85) Does an 85 gt have a recall on it?
Z||000007||Patrick||08-21-99||12:01 AM||||<br>Has there ever been a car made that DIDN'T have a recall on it? Seriously?<p>
Z||000008||theogre||08-21-99||03:23 PM||||ALL Fiero are subject to at least 1 recall. some, earlier ones, had more.<p>check the site I listed above to see what they were. Only GM/Pontiac can tell you if they were done or not. Theya re suposed to apply a decal when they do repairs but they often fall off.
Z||000009||Bruce||08-21-99||06:52 PM||||All the manifolds and heat shields should be replaced by recall order. Also, there were some brake caliper and e-brake problems, at least up to 86. Don't wait around to get it done!!
Z||000010||mshill||08-23-99||03:58 PM||||Ok, I just purchased an 86 SE V6 on Saturday.<br>I believe I am the third owner.  I was about<br>to embark on an engine rebuild when I found<br>this thread.<p>Is it my responsibility to prove the recall <br>work has not been done? or the Dealers?<p>Should I wait to rebuild?<p>Thanks for the help?<p>Mark S.
Z||000011||theogre||08-23-99||04:30 PM||||you need to call to make sure if pontiac has the recall work on file. If they say it was done, and you don't think it was, good luck proving otherwise.<p>call more than one dealler.
Z||000012||mshill||08-24-99||05:41 PM||||Well, I have called three dealers and all <br>three say "The GM database shows no open <br>campaigns for your car (VIN)".<p>When I asked them if I could find out when the<br>work had been done, they said all the <br>database showed was there were "no open<br>campaigns".  It doesn't say when and where<br>the work may have been done.  <p>I called 1-800-PMCARES the woman on the other<br>end told me the database only went back to <br>1996.<p>So, what database are the dealers looking<br>at?<p>What's my next step.  I am certain that the <br>manifold work has not been done, and I cannot<br>keep the car in my driveway without chocks<br>because of the emergency brake.<p>Mark S.
Z||000013||mshill||08-24-99||06:07 PM||||Just got off the phone with 1-800-PMCARES, and this time I got someone willing to help me out a bit.<p>The database they have goes back nine years. So again, she indicated that a run of the VIN would not show any open campaigns.  However, she suggested that I take the campaign bulletins with me to the dealership and the car and they would be able to tell if they had been done by inspecting the car.<p>So I will be doing this in the next couple of days.
Z||000014||Bruce||08-24-99||06:18 PM||||Call the dealer in my area: Putnam Pontiac,<br>650-342-4321. They were really good about providing recall info for me and doing the corrections. At any rate, they should be able to provide you with the recall status of your Fiero.<p>
